-- The form is docs/language-derived-from-the-record.cub's, for texts read by the checker:
-- (§3) a context selects, of the meanings a text may have, a fiber: the reading of the text;
-- (§4, §6) the reading is determinate, the notation theorem-grade, exactly when that fiber is
-- contractible; (§11) scope is the context; and printing is the same relation read the other way,
-- the fiber of texts over a meaning. A notation is a standpoint: every notation, the reader's own
-- included, relates texts to the one type of meanings, and none is the hub through which another is
-- read. In the machine (src/syntax.c, p_decl_in) a block of a file is written
--
--   syntax N
--     any lines, indented past the syntax line
--
-- and N, a checked reading List Word → Lst Meaning, gives the block's meaning: declarations, each a
-- name with the codes of its type and its value (lib/code.cub). The checker checks each as it checks
-- anything written, so a notation is trusted for nothing: a wrong one gives a meaning that does not
-- check.
import "core.cub"

